:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Docs",
    title: "Plugin Reference",
    summary: "Built-in plugins cover Ruby, Haml, Markdown, CSS, assets, data imports, routing, and Google Fonts."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Default Plugin Set" }
    :markdown
      `Klenod::Build::Context.default_plugins` includes `RubyPlugin`, `IntlPlugin`, `HamlPlugin`, `MarkdownPlugin`, `CssPlugin`, `SvgPlugin`, `ImagePlugin`, `JsonPlugin`, `YamlPlugin`, `TomlPlugin`, and `TextPlugin`.

      `RouterPlugin` and `GoogleFontsPlugin` are built in but opt-in.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Hook Phases" }
    :markdown
      Plugins can implement:

      - `resolve(dependency, context)` to map an import specifier to a module id.
      - `load(module_id, context)` to provide source for virtual or custom modules.
      - `transform(module_id, code, context)` to rewrite source and record dependencies, assets, metadata, source maps, and watched patterns.
      - `finalize(module_id, result, resolved_dependencies, dependency_records, context)` to adjust a transform after eager dependency records are collected.
      - `import_value(resolved_dependency, record, context)` to provide development-time import values.
      - `runtime_import_value(resolved_dependency, record, context)` to provide serialized bundle import values.

      `resolve`, `load`, `transform`, and `finalize` are collection-time hooks. They must not depend on evaluated app exports. `runtime_import_value` must return serializable values or runtime instructions.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Core Plugins" }
    :markdown
      - `RubyPlugin` handles `.rb`, rewrites `import`, `lazy_import`, and `import_glob`, and records Ruby dependencies.
      - `HamlPlugin` handles `.haml`, generates component classes, rewrites Haml imports, tracks CSS and intl companions, and emits source maps.
      - `MarkdownPlugin` handles `.md` modules and Haml `:markdown` filters.
      - `CssPlugin` scopes CSS, emits stylesheet assets, returns class-name maps to Ruby/Haml, and records CSS dependencies.
      - `SvgPlugin` emits SVG assets with dimensions.
      - `ImagePlugin` emits raster source assets and generated variants.
      - `IntlPlugin` parses Haml companion translation files.
      - `JsonPlugin`, `YamlPlugin`, `TomlPlugin`, and `TextPlugin` import structured data and text.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Opt-In Plugins" }
    :markdown
      `RouterPlugin` discovers filesystem route modules and generates `virtual:router`.

      ```ruby
      Klenod::Build::Plugins::RouterPlugin.new(
        specifier: "virtual:router",
        pages_dir: "pages",
        extensions: [".rb", ".haml"]
      )
      ```

      `GoogleFontsPlugin` resolves Google Fonts CSS imports, rewrites font URLs to local assets, and can cache raw Google CSS responses.

      ```ruby
      Klenod::Build::Plugins::GoogleFontsPlugin.new(
        cache_path: "tmp/cache/google_fonts"
      )
      ```
